{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/951193-question-about-the-first-city","id":951193,"title":"Question about the First City","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-15T10:37:21-07:00","id":951193,"title":"Question about the First City","content":"In a couple of places in W20 Changing Breeds, it mentions that the Garou were allied with their Kin in the First City during the War of Rage. is this the same as Enoch, the First City, from Vampire: the Masquerade? The time frame seems about right. It would be odd for Garou to be allied with vampires, but war makes strange bedfellows...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T11:33:24-07:00","id":951219,"title":"","content":"I prefer not to mix the mythologies of Vampire and Werewolf because the result does not make any bloody sense. In essence, you either have to go with the mythology of Vampires, which is a non-scientific theistic mythology that accepts the Creation Myth of the Abrahamic religions, or with the mythology of Werewolf, which is a scientific spiritual mythology that accepts that the Earth is billions of years old and accepts that evolution occurred over the course of hundreds of millions of years (even if the Garou believe that it was guided by Gaia and the Triat). Since I am scientifically literate and accept the fact of evolution and the four billion year plus existence of the Earth, I favor the mythology of Werewolf over the mythology of Vampire. In fact, I favor the mythology of Werewolf over every other mythology in the World of Darkness because none of the other mythologies seem to accept the fact of evolution or the four billion year plus existence of the Earth, so I think that they are objectively wrong, whether it is Changeling, Mage, Vampire, Wraith, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T11:45:57-07:00","id":951222,"title":"","content":"Aya Tari: You raise a good point, and one that I have addressed in my Crossover Timeline. However, the question I asked is a more specific one: were the writers of W20 Changing Breeds intending to refer to the First City of Vampire when they referred to an alliance between the Garou and the First City, or is it just a coincidence in names? My personal theory is that it is not a coincidence, and that the Garou did indeed forge an alliance with vampires against the other Changing Breeds, but I wanted to see what others on the forums thought about this. Based on your objection to mixing Werewolf with Vampire, I assume you are saying no, it's not the same city. Like I said, you raise a good point. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T14:01:28-07:00","id":951302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/951193-question-about-the-first-city?p=951219#post951219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I prefer not to mix the mythologies of Vampire and Werewolf because the result does not make any bloody sense. In essence, you either have to go with the mythology of Vampires, which is a non-scientific theistic mythology that accepts the Creation Myth of the Abrahamic religions, or with the mythology of Werewolf, which is a scientific spiritual mythology that accepts that the Earth is billions of years old and accepts that evolution occurred over the course of hundreds of millions of years (even if the Garou believe that it was guided by Gaia and the Triat).</div> </div> </div> </div>I love Werewolf, but it is not scientific, at all. If your only criteria for having a scientific accuracy is the age of the earth, that could be easily changed in all the other game lines. Make the First City take place a lot longer ago, change the dates of the Deluge to whatever you want, have Caine be a murderous non-human hominid, it doesn't matter. It just seems really stupid to get hung on this one point when it is so easily fixed. Jettisoning the other game settings because New Earth is horrible science is throwing the baby out with the bathwater.<br /> <br /> @Julian, do whatever you want. Figuring where the First City fits into the Impergium could be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 08-15-2016, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T16:02:30-07:00","id":951357,"title":"","content":"Shattered Dreams covers this best.. and the only Vampires who show up.. well they don't talk about Caine or Enoch or Generations. We do know where Mount Meru is though!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T17:22:15-07:00","id":951395,"title":"","content":"I use the end of the Ice Age as a firm cut off point. The Antedeluvian world occurred before the end of the Ice Age, and the Garou were not around then. The Deluge happened, and then the &quot;real&quot; world began. So the Garou and Changing Breeds became &quot;born&quot; sometimes around 12,000-10,000 BC. At some point after that the Antedeluvians recovered from the Deluge and founded the Second City. Thousands of years after that, they went into torpor and disappeared and the Methusalehs they left behind were in charge.<br /> <br /> The Second City might still have been around during the War of Rage, but it really depends on how you define it. Since typically the War of Rage is supposed to be after the Imperium, I hold that the Second City was long gone by then. The childer of the Antedeluvians were still the Mesopotamian god-kings, and it is highly unlikely the Garou had any involvement with the cities because of it. At most, they were minimal. I believe one of the reasons the Impergium was instituted was because the local Garou in Mesopotamia could see what happens when agricultural surpluses lead to cities and dense populations.<br /> <br /> In practice, I think the &quot;War of Rage&quot; didn't happen in the way the books try to portray it. No Garou at that time thought there was a War of Rage going in. It is a term developed by Garou historians many, many, many years afterwards (probably in the post-Classical world). At the time, it was just the kind of sporadic, but ongoing warfare primitive societies always fought. It is just that after a long enough time, all these local fights actually succeeded in driving some of the Changing Breeds into extinction, or greatly depleted their numbers.<br /> <br /> Typically, I find a lot of development done after the original corebooks to be very poor. Sometimes there are good ideas, and sometimes there are bad ideas. I take what I like and ignore the rest. No reason to keep so much canon when so much of it is bad, inconsistent with each other, or just isn't my taste.<br /> <br /> Saying that Garou allied with vampires to kill the other Changing Breeds is probably just propaganda from the other breeds so they have yet something else to accuse people they don't like. Ignore it if you want. If you like the idea, then keep it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T20:34:57-07:00","id":951471,"title":"","content":"To me it sounds like the Garou did not ally with the Kindred. Just their kinfolk that LIVED in the Kindred city, the First City. Second I could see the War of Rage being a literal war. But back then the people didn't know what war was. I can see the Garou hunting down any Changing Breed members in their territory. Actively hunting. And when it was brought To their attention, forming a war party and going to destroy a Changing Breed villages. But that's just me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T21:16:29-07:00","id":951480,"title":"","content":"Even in Vampire Enoch isn't LITTERALLY the first city humans ever made. Its the first city of Vampires. It isn't even treated as the sole pre Flood city. Nor is the Second City treated as a post Deluvian Babel afterwards even in the most litteral readings of Noddist lore. I am pretty sure we wouldn't have Glasswalkers if the first city was founded by Open Wyrm Godkings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T02:37:41-07:00","id":951569,"title":"","content":"Thanks to everyone who posted, especially Lian. This is really helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T06:32:21-07:00","id":951654,"title":"","content":"The Garou existed before the end of the last Ice Age. Otherwise, their Kinfolk would not have crossed to the Americas with the Native Americans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T08:20:04-07:00","id":951725,"title":"","content":"Garou date back to at least the height of the ice age, with no indication anywhere they don't predate it entirely. Where did you find anything to the contrary, Black Fox?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T08:39:35-07:00","id":951738,"title":"","content":"I believe Black Fox is giving personal vision vs canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T08:48:00-07:00","id":951750,"title":"","content":"Why people feel compelled to give their fanon in threads asking about a canon fact is beyond me. Reasonable conjecture is one thing, but to go about posting 'well in MY version...' when it has no real relationship to the topic at hand is another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T11:17:43-07:00","id":951855,"title":"","content":"And the Rokea and the Mokole, which are Changing Breeds, predate the Ice Age by around 250 million years at least because they evolved with, or before, the first dinosaurs. Heck,it is suggest that the Gurahl created the last Ice Age, so they definitely predate the last Ice Age. The only 'new' Changing Breed is the Kitsune.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T14:34:09-07:00","id":952034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/951193-question-about-the-first-city?p=951750#post951750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why people feel compelled to give their fanon in threads asking about a canon fact is beyond me. Reasonable conjecture is one thing, but to go about posting 'well in MY version...' when it has no real relationship to the topic at hand is another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotta call you out on that. Dude's asking about the First City with regards to an ancient VtM/WtA crossover. There isn't cannon answers here. If you gotta make something up, might as well hear what others are doing, cannon be damned. At least in this case, I want to hear alternatives, even if they are not bog-standard Apocalypse... because a bog-standard WtA setting generally doesn't include the First City.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T16:55:11-07:00","id":952135,"title":"","content":"Dude's asking 'is it the same city', not 'tell me all your tangentially related fanon'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T18:25:55-07:00","id":952188,"title":"","content":"You<i> can</i> post 'fannon' however 'tangentially' related; making up stuff is what RPGs is about, after all. Calling someone else's game fannon betrays that you think there is some greater cannon that should be adhered to. Telling people to can it when they mention that they *just might* play in a slightly different universe than the Holy God-Ordained Cannon is not helpful and far more damaging to overall discourse.<br /> <br /> You aren't a mod, you aren't an arbitrator of what is on topic, and the notion that we need to cleave to some vaunted cannon or risk being irrelevant is terribly unhelpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 08-16-2016, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T18:36:04-07:00","id":952191,"title":"","content":"I'm not saying you can't. What I am saying is that it isn't always appropriate, and when the topic is 'is the first city referenced in &lt;x product&gt; the same one as in &lt;y gameline&gt;?', throwing out a bunch of fanon tangentially related to that question and strongly divergent from the actual canon is <i>unhelpful</i>.<br /> <br /> As for calling it fanon? That's what it is. There's canon - what we see presented in the actual books and materials - and there's everything else we create, which is by definition not canonical. There is absolutely no problem with diverging from canon in your games, but when questions are about the canonical status of something, it isn't time to post the ways you diverge. This is a fairly straight forward proposition and I don't understand why you're getting so aggressive about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T18:39:03-07:00","id":952192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/951193-question-about-the-first-city?p=952188#post952188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You<i> can</i> post 'fannon' however 'tangentially' related; making up stuff is what RPGs is about, after all. Calling someone else's game fannon betrays that you think there is some greater cannon that should be adhered to. Telling people to can it when they mention that they *just might* play in a slightly different universe than the Holy God-Ordained Cannon is not helpful and far more damaging to overall discourse.<br /> <br /> You aren't a mod, you aren't an arbitrator of what is on topic, and the notion that we need to cleave to some vaunted cannon or risk being irrelevant is terribly unhelpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just posting in support of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3695_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3695\" data-vbnamecard=\"3695\">The Laughing Stranger</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>. Really, anything dealing with the First City is going to be made up at individual tables since there is what....2 references in the books and no write up?<br /> Stuff like this is why I try and preface anything I write on here with whether or not my posts are from memory, or from the books or wholly made up.<br /> <br /> In any case, I prefer not to have my Werewolf &quot;First City&quot; have anything to do with Vampire's &quot;First City&quot; Enoch. I would find a hard time reconciling the 2 and have a coherent historical timeline that makes sense given what both lines have to say about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T18:57:35-07:00","id":952198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/951193-question-about-the-first-city?p=951855#post951855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the Rokea and the Mokole, which are Changing Breeds, predate the Ice Age by around 250 million years at least because they evolved with, or before, the first dinosaurs. Heck,it is suggest that the Gurahl created the last Ice Age, so they definitely predate the last Ice Age. The only 'new' Changing Breed is the Kitsune.</div> </div> </div> </div>And even they aren't really that young, since their first major action - or rather, the first major action of the White-Faced One - was to take down the Shang Dynasty, and they had to have existed long enough to get someone who was far beyond legendary rank established.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T19:01:56-07:00","id":952200,"title":"","content":"Yes, the Changing Breeds are more ancient than any other supernatural race.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T19:50:27-07:00","id":952226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/951193-question-about-the-first-city?p=952200#post952200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, the Changing Breeds are more ancient than any other supernatural race.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that's pretty subjective. All of the splats at some level go back &quot;to the beginning&quot; and placing them on a timeline against each other is pretty much going to come down to conjecture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T20:15:29-07:00","id":952238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/951193-question-about-the-first-city?p=952226#post952226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue that's pretty subjective. All of the splats at some level go back &quot;to the beginning&quot; and placing them on a timeline against each other is pretty much going to come down to conjecture.</div> </div> </div> </div>Queue the following argument: But Mokole are dinosaurs and were around millions of years ago.<br /> <br /> The different game's histories weren't really meant o be compared alongside each other.<br /> <br /> Edit: in anything but the broadest (and highly subjective) strokes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T20:24:17-07:00","id":952243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/951193-question-about-the-first-city?p=952238#post952238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Queue the following argument: But Mokole are dinosaurs and were around millions of years ago.<br /> <br /> The different game's histories weren't really meant o be compared alongside each other.<br /> <br /> Edit: in anything but the broadest (and highly subjective) strokes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its true, &quot;Which magical man came first&quot; doesn't really add anything to the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T21:35:25-07:00","id":952284,"title":"","content":"No where in Vampire does it say Caine invented Cities. He isn't treated as a Cultural hero who brings civilization to wild mankind He just seems other cities and thinks &quot;Hey i want to stop wandering I'm super powerful I'm going to rule there!&quot; The only place where Enoch is implied to be particularly revoluationary(outside being ruled by vampires) Is in Demon where it might have been the first city not run by Demons.. but you try placing Demon timeline with Werewolf its not going to be pretty.<br /> <br /> Masquerade Vampires aren't brought up at all in Shattered Dreams(Wan Kuei are though!) so take that for as little or as much as how much Enoch effected Fera society. We even have a period in said book called the Deluge. There are no Kindred, or at least weren't any as shown in the manuscript that was seen by the backers. They may have added some since then, but as of right now there's no connection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T23:53:56-07:00","id":952360,"title":"","content":"Demon kind of have the claim to pre-date Creation, so...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T00:03:48-07:00","id":952365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/951193-question-about-the-first-city?p=952360#post952360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon kind of have the claim to pre-date Creation, so...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mean Cities of Demons. I mean cities of Humans but Run by Demons. That's where Enoch is closer to being something special since it possibly the first city not run by a Demon or Angel and might be the only one During the War of Wrath.<br /> <br /> But that doesn't match up with anything Werewolf related anymore than Etherites talking about Cayce's Atlantis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T11:13:55-07:00","id":952628,"title":"","content":"Yes, but their Creation is only 6,000 years old, and every Changing Breed other than the Kitsune predates their Creation by tens of thousands, if not hundreds of millions, of years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T14:44:12-07:00","id":952748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/951193-question-about-the-first-city?p=952284#post952284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No where in Vampire does it say Caine invented Cities. He isn't treated as a Cultural hero who brings civilization to wild mankind He just seems other cities and thinks &quot;Hey i want to stop wandering I'm super powerful I'm going to rule there!&quot; The only place where Enoch is implied to be particularly revoluationary(outside being ruled by vampires) Is in Demon where it might have been the first city not run by Demons.. but you try placing Demon timeline with Werewolf its not going to be pretty.<br /> <br /> Masquerade Vampires aren't brought up at all in Shattered Dreams(Wan Kuei are though!) so take that for as little or as much as how much Enoch effected Fera society. We even have a period in said book called the Deluge. There are no Kindred, or at least weren't any as shown in the manuscript that was seen by the backers. They may have added some since then, but as of right now there's no connection.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Also important to note that the great flood in Shattered dreams is the flooding of Doggerland, and not any flooding of the Fertile Crescent...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T14:57:51-07:00","id":952758,"title":"","content":"Though there is archeological evidence that the flooding of the land beneath the Persian Gulf occurred during the same time period, and it had an area over 12 times as large as Doggerland.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T14:59:53-07:00","id":952760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/951193-question-about-the-first-city?p=952758#post952758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though there is archeological evidence that the flooding of the land beneath the Persian Gulf occurred during the same time period, and it had an area over 12 times as large as Doggerland.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which is fine, but that's not the area that's in Shattered Dreams. The google doc write up specifically stated Doggerland. Now if you want to change things so it could be Enoch, I don't see anything wrong with that (I have a Mokole PC with the flood gift, and I was really really really tempted to make that change in Shattered Dreams only because I know he'd have a blast being the reason for the flooding of Enoch).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T15:03:15-07:00","id":952763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/951193-question-about-the-first-city?p=952628#post952628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but their Creation is only 6,000 years old, and every Changing Breed other than the Kitsune predates their Creation by tens of thousands, if not hundreds of millions, of years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if you assume that being part of Biblical pre-history means they cannot be older than six millennia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T15:10:37-07:00","id":952770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/951193-question-about-the-first-city?p=952763#post952763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only if you assume that being part of Biblical pre-history means they cannot be older than six millennia.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e6/Creation_Museum_10.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Check mate in favor of Cain and his buddies!<br /> IGNORE MOKOLE PROPAGANDA!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T17:25:54-07:00","id":952872,"title":"","content":"If you believe in the literal truth of the Bible, everything is only 6,000 years old (which is kind of a prerequisite if you believe in Abrahamic angels, demons, Creation, etc). If you accept science, everything is much, much older and the Changing Breeds probably have a better handle on history than the Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T18:09:51-07:00","id":952897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/951193-question-about-the-first-city?p=952872#post952872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you believe in the literal truth of the Bible, everything is only 6,000 years old (which is kind of a prerequisite if you believe in Abrahamic angels, demons, Creation, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, this is just wrongheaded. Catholicism, the largest branch of Christianity, does not view the biblical account as supporting a 6000 or 10,000 year timeline. Many, many Christians (myself included) do not consider the Old Testament to be scientifically literate by 20th century standards, and believe that the earth is far, far older than Kenny Ham et al want it to be. The genealogies are not complete, and the account in Genesis is poetic symbolism, and the flood wasn't the cause of the Grand Canyon.<br /> <br /> With that out of the way, in our rpg scenario, God and his angels (and demons or messengers, whatever) can make the earth billions of years ago and Caine can be a homo-habilus. Alternatively the first vampire could have just crabbed the biblical account or made it up whole cloth, if that floats your ark. Maybe Caine was indeed cursed by a middle-eastern deity for being the first murderer but he was not actually the third human on the planet and he was cursed by Namtar, not Yahweh.<br /> <br /> My point is that it is so, so easy to come up with stories that include Caine or angels or whatever elements we need for a WtA/VtM crossover without having a 6000 year-old earth narrative; your inability to move past this reminds me of a warning issued by Ralph Waldo Emerson regarding foolish consistencies.<br /> <br /> tl;dr Checkmate, Scientologists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T18:52:54-07:00","id":952912,"title":"","content":"As I said, the literal truth of the Bible, because people who believe in the literal truth of the Bible believe in the Creation (the capital 'C' refers to the literal interpretation of the Bible, a small 'c' or 'Abrahamic Creation Myth' would have been used if I was referring to a non-literal interpretation). For people who do not believe in the literal truth of the Bible, there is flexibility and many of them attempt to combine religion with science because they accept science. People who believe that Genesis is poetic symbolism are by definition flexible, which is appropriate considering that Genesis was not formulated until the 6th century, probably after the Babylonian exile, and is considered to be an allegory by the majority of Jewish religious scholars (the majority of Christian religious scholars also come on the side of it being an allegory as well). <br /> <br /> On another note, Caine could not have been Homo Habilus. Homo Habilus went extinct around 2 million years ago and, even before then, was not that much smarter than a six year old child. Even under the most liberal interpretations of the timeline of Caine, he would have had to have been born anywhere from 15,000 BC to 12,000 BC if he was a historical entity. I do not think that any of the Mokole, however, mention memories of anyone by the name Caine being existent around that time, though they could not have met everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T18:56:38-07:00","id":952914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/951193-question-about-the-first-city?p=952872#post952872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you believe in the literal truth of the Bible, everything is only 6,000 years old (which is kind of a prerequisite if you believe in Abrahamic angels, demons, Creation, etc). If you accept science, everything is much, much older and the Changing Breeds probably have a better handle on history than the Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter is not in any way predicated on the former, especially in a fictional universe where the latter objectively exists. I'm assuming you don't believe that because Demons exist the universe is automatically six millennia old, therefore why in a universe that is billions of years old does everything with an Abrahamic basis only appear six millennia ago? <br /> <br /> Also, Changing Breeds pretty forfeits any claim to a scientific outlook considering how much it relies on, you know, nature spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T20:13:34-07:00","id":952951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/951193-question-about-the-first-city?p=952284#post952284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No where in Vampire does it say Caine invented Cities. He isn't treated as a Cultural hero who brings civilization to wild mankind</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but the Book of Nod says Caine invented Agriculture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T21:58:10-07:00","id":952984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/951193-question-about-the-first-city?p=952951#post952951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, but the Book of Nod says Caine invented Agriculture.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I can't imagine why a book written by vampires (or even the first vampire if we're being orthodox) would want to make vampires feel self-important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T22:26:18-07:00","id":952990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/951193-question-about-the-first-city?p=951219#post951219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">....I favor the mythology of Werewolf over the mythology of Vampire. In fact, I favor the mythology of Werewolf over every other mythology in the World of Darkness <b>because none of the other mythologies seem to accept the fact of evolution or the four billion year plus existence of the Earth</b>, so I think that they are objectively wrong, whether it is Changeling, Mage, Vampire, Wraith, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/951193-question-about-the-first-city?p=952872#post952872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you believe in the literal truth of the Bible, everything is only 6,000 years old (which is kind of a prerequisite if you believe in Abrahamic angels, demons, Creation, etc). If you accept science, everything is much, much older and the Changing Breeds probably have a better handle on history than the Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That doesn't hold as entirely true in the classic world of Darkness since the Creation Myth is nicely addressed in Demon: The Fallen (page 25 of Demon: The Fallen's corebook: Paradise) as being:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While Matthew busied himself with coffee, Noahwent to the bathroom. When they had resumed theirseats, Matthew frowned and asked a question.<br /> \u201cWhat was Paradise like?\u201d<br /> <br /> Noah folded his hands and frowned.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re not very well equipped to understand it,\u201d he said at last. \u201cI don\u2019t say that to be insulting. The world wasfundamentally different back then. It was... more complex. Richer. It had layers that are simply absent, now.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLayers?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes... consider this coffee we\u2019re drinking. It\u2019s only coffee, right?\u201c t's not anything else?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I guess not.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIn the uncorrupted world, this coffee could alsoexist simultaneously as a song or an aesthetic idea oreven a sentient and helpful creature. Different thingson different layers, all equally real, all similar, but each discrete - even while they were simultaneously experienced.\u201d Seeing Matthew\u2019s expression, he continued.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll give you a more relevant example. The firstpeople: Were they Adam and Eve, a woman and a man,or were they the evolved descendents of apes?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey were a woman and a man, as the Bible says.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCorrect. But they were also a multitude of ape descendents. The universe was made in seven days, on one level, but that same span of time was billions ofyears on another level.<br /> <br /> \u201cOr consider the Angels of the Firmament. On some levels of reality they were conveying the life-giving breath of the Maker on a purely scientific level - they were, literally were, the process by which solar energystriking simple carbon molecules agitated them intoforms of ever increasing complexity, until they becameorganic molecules, then primitive single-celledanimals,then nucleated cells and so on, up to and including dogs,cats and humans. But at the same time they were crouchingover the mouths of newly sculpted creatures of all types,breathing into their mouths to animate them.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you talking about metaphor?\u201d<br /> <br /> Gaviel chuckled. &quot;Not yet, no. These contrary thingsreally were simultaneously true in the young cosmos. Itmakes no sense to you because you\u2019re used to living in this,the singular world. But once you accept the idea of themultiple world, it clears up a lot of the problemsyou humanshave with faith, miracles, the Divine Architect-''<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t have any problems with my faith.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNone? Well, you should. Can an omnipotentbeing create a boulder so big he can\u2019t lift it?\u201d <br /> <br /> Matthew dismissed the thought with an irritatedwave of his hand. \u201cOh, here we go... Are you trying to shake my faith again? Because it\u2019s going to take a lotmore than that tired old chestnut.\u201d<br /> <br /> [...] </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12152-rotwood","name":"Rotwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T23:02:28-07:00","id":953002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/951193-question-about-the-first-city?p=952914#post952914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The latter is not in any way predicated on the former, especially in a fictional universe where the latter objectively exists. I'm assuming you don't believe that because Demons exist the universe is automatically six millennia old, therefore why in a universe that is billions of years old does everything with an Abrahamic basis only appear six millennia ago?<br /> <br /> Also, Changing Breeds pretty forfeits any claim to a scientific outlook considering how much it relies on, you know, nature spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf operates on a peculiar wavelength that incorporates findings of modern evidence into its narrative. It adds spirits onto this, rather than outright replacing it like some other games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rotwood</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That doesn't hold as entirely true in the classic world of Darkness since the Creation Myth is nicely addressed in Demon: The Fallen (page 25 of Demon: The Fallen's corebook: Paradise) as being:</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Which is all nice and well for Demon, but it doesn't begin to approach welding anything together. It's a cop-out hiding behind the excuse of &quot;divine being says shut up.&quot;</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T23:49:14-07:00","id":953016,"title":"","content":"Every version of the book of Nod I've seen comes off as something akin to the book of Mormon or Book of Jubilees. Something clearly written much later and meant to explain stuff.. now this is because on a Doyalist that's exactly what it is.<br /> <br /> Caine and the First city are myths it may be based on something but its really only as of the Second City we start to see anything resembling a dawning of Kindred history and even that is spotty at best.<br /> <br /> Even then Kindred don't come into play in the changeing breed calendar until Set shows in Egypt(Score one for Typhonist mythology!) Of course.. we also have the &quot;Ravana&quot; thing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T00:51:45-07:00","id":953027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/951193-question-about-the-first-city?p=952872#post952872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you believe in the literal truth of the Bible, everything is only 6,000 years old (which is kind of a prerequisite if you believe in Abrahamic angels, demons, Creation, etc). If you accept science, everything is much, much older and the Changing Breeds probably have a better handle on history than the Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only reason this figure is a thing is that a bishop named Ussher sat down, made some assumptions, and worked it out based on the only information available at the time - the Bible and extrabiblical Christian and Judaic texts that tackled the issue before Ussher set out the 'gold standard' of creation dating. Church fathers like Origen and Augustine rejected any such view in their time, and revered figures found hugely different potential dates both before and after Ussher. The belief in a young earth is not a prerequisite for an Abrahamic faith, nor is it in any way a necessary consequence of believing the 'literal truth' of the Bible because there are large periods of time which are undated and provide no possible time references to reinforce or contradict any given age of the Earth beyond a bare minimum - we could use that 4004BC figure as a <i>minimum</i> date, but to declare with certainty that is when Creation took place ignores these uncertain periods. Nor is a young earth mainstream dogma for Anglicans, Lutherans, Catholics, or a myriad of other Christian denominations - all of whom believe quite strongly in Creation as a divine act.<br /> <br /> It is, however, a necessary conclusion that if the account in Demon <i>is</i> accurate to the greater WoD (I am not stating it to be so, merely stating a logical conclusion) and the time of that Creation is 6000 years then, as the cosmos was forged by God and Her servants at that time, all things must postdate that creation and any claim to the contrary by Changing Breeds is an inherently false proposition. You can't really have 'Demons only created existence in 4004BC but there were mokole before that'. The two statements are fundamentally incompatible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On another note, Caine could not have been Homo Habilus. Homo Habilus went extinct around 2 million years ago and, even before then, was not that much smarter than a six year old child. Even under the most liberal interpretations of the timeline of Caine, he would have had to have been born anywhere from 15,000 BC to 12,000 BC if he was a historical entity. I do not think that any of the Mokole, however, mention memories of anyone by the name Caine being existent around that time, though they could not have met everyone. </div> </div> </div>[/quote]<br /> <br /> Peking Man was preyed on by vampires. It's in an officially published and licensed product (though one is tempted to tie it in with the existence of homid Ananasi circa 98000BC.)<br /> <br /> More seriously, there is nothing in the timeline of Caine to suggest that he must necessarily postdate 15000BC other than 'agriculture' and 'cities', which given the Impergium as an option and the pre-solidified concept of reality being in flux, aren't really all that definitive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/951193-question-about-the-first-city?p=953002#post953002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werewolf operates on a peculiar wavelength that incorporates findings of modern evidence into its narrative. It adds spirits onto this, rather than outright replacing it like some other games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always viewed it the other way around. Werewolf is, at its core, not a scientific game. It adds science to strengthen its narrative where it wants, but is based on its own mythopoetia rather than scientic facts and favours its own mythopoetia over science when the two conflict irreconcilably. So, it's more 'werewolf adds science onto this' than 'werewolf adds spirits onto this' in my view.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T04:57:49-07:00","id":953100,"title":"","content":"I think that Werewolf is more willing to accept science and to incorporate it into its narrative than Mage or Vampire (Changeling and Wraith just avoid the issue entirely). Spirits are not unscientific, they do not particularly preclude any scientific principles, they are ascientific, meaning that they are just outside of conventional scientific theory. It was not that long ago that electromagnetic and thermodynamic phenomena were also ascientific, as they were unexplainable under Newtonian physics. I have seen quite sophisticated physics models that would allow for spiritual entities and multiple planes of existence, but we simply lack the tools to test their hypotheses (we cannot even get fusion right yet, so we are still kind of primitive technologically, though we have good video games).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T05:33:49-07:00","id":953110,"title":"","content":"If we are going to get into Science, why do Mokole have connections to dinosaurs when Corax/tengu are actually scientifically the Dinosaur breed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T06:31:41-07:00","id":953129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/951193-question-about-the-first-city?p=953100#post953100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that Werewolf is more willing to accept science and to incorporate it into its narrative than Mage or Vampire (Changeling and Wraith just avoid the issue entirely). Spirits are not unscientific, they do not particularly preclude any scientific principles, they are ascientific, meaning that they are just outside of conventional scientific theory. It was not that long ago that electromagnetic and thermodynamic phenomena were also ascientific, as they were unexplainable under Newtonian physics. I have seen quite sophisticated physics models that would allow for spiritual entities and multiple planes of existence, but we simply lack the tools to test their hypotheses (we cannot even get fusion right yet, so we are still kind of primitive technologically, though we have good video games).</div> </div> </div> </div>If it falls outside of conventional scientific theory or accepted scientific consensus, cannot be tested with the scientific method, and can in fact be disproven by the scientific method - and Werewolf's take on spiritual entities <i>absolutely can be disproven</i> <i>in reality</i> - then it's not 'ascientific', but actively unscientific. This is not a problem thematically, but it does mean that the basic conceits of the setting - the existence of spirits entities capable of physical manifestation in this material reality, the existence of three creator-spirits/sentient creator-forces, the existence of the Garou as a genetically distinguishable population, the ability of a Garou to gain or lose weight while shapeshifting, the ability to walk into an alternate universe by looking in a mirror, the existence of the soul as a distinct and quantifiable thing, etc - are in and of themselves hostile to the viewpoint that Werewolf is somehow built on science, not fantasy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T06:58:46-07:00","id":953140,"title":"","content":"Let us take the conservation of mass problem. If the Umbra is an equal but separate plane, there will likely be things that correspond to matter and energy. By transferring Umbra matter to the physical plane, you can make up for the change in mass without violating any laws of physics, you are simply working on a more fundamental level of physics than even quantum physics. The fact the the Changing Breeds revert to their breed form at death supports the idea of borrowing matter, as nothing is permanently added to the physical plane. If you want things that are blatantly unscientific, look at Mage rather than Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T07:06:30-07:00","id":953144,"title":"","content":"Except of course that the Umbra, as presented in Werewolf, is <i>also</i> unscientific - thus, any theory that relies on 'mass borrowing' from the Umbra falls apart as 'scientific'. Not only do you first have to present the Umbra in a scientifically possible light, but you have to have reasonable, explained, quantifiable models of how that borrowing takes place - and we don't. This is one of the major differences in science fiction and fantasy (even when it uses SF trappings.) In science fiction, the deviation points need to be explored, modelled, and treated as being a scientific reality. In fantasy, none of that needs to be done because it isn't science, it's magic. Werewolf belongs to the latter category, not the former, as the deviation points are of a mystical nature and can only be explained by means of mysticism, not by anything we know as science.<br /> <br /> If you want a science based game, look somewhere other than the game about playing literal werewolves fighting a cosmic holy war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T07:49:18-07:00","id":953168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/951193-question-about-the-first-city?p=953110#post953110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we are going to get into Science, why do Mokole have connections to dinosaurs when Corax/tengu are actually scientifically the Dinosaur breed?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mokole actually had non-avian dinosaurs as kin (and attendant varnas) before the Wonder-Work of the Dissolver, and retain connections to everything that they remember.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T07:51:19-07:00","id":953172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/951193-question-about-the-first-city?p=953144#post953144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except of course that the Umbra, as presented in Werewolf, is <i>also</i> unscientific - thus, any theory that relies on 'mass borrowing' from the Umbra falls apart as 'scientific'. Not only do you first have to present the Umbra in a scientifically possible light, but you have to have reasonable, explained, quantifiable models of how that borrowing takes place - and we don't. This is one of the major differences in science fiction and fantasy (even when it uses SF trappings.) In science fiction, the deviation points need to be explored, modelled, and treated as being a scientific reality. In fantasy, none of that needs to be done because it isn't science, it's magic. Werewolf belongs to the latter category, not the former, as the deviation points are of a mystical nature and can only be explained by means of mysticism, not by anything we know as science.<br /> <br /> If you want a science based game, look somewhere other than the game about playing literal werewolves fighting a cosmic holy war.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Umbra is a weird part. The material world isn't, and often, the antagonists are presented as not engaging in ethical or advisable practice of scholarly inquiry, ignoring things in front of their face or relying on outdated or discredited information.<br /> <br /> (Also, the primary reason that scientists can't test the Umbra is because it's not readily open to humans, unless they wander through the heart of a caern, and no one's going to live to tell that tale. The other reason is because one of the many conspiracies in a conspiracy game is that the existence of such a thing is suppressed, and anyone trying to go against the grain ends up thrown out of the practice to save face.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 08-18-2016, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T07:55:54-07:00","id":953175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/951193-question-about-the-first-city?p=953168#post953168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Mokole actually had non-avian dinosaurs as kin (and attendant varnas) before the Wonder-Work of the Dissolver, and retain connections to everything that they remember.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would say that's not based on any particular science out there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T07:57:00-07:00","id":953176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/951193-question-about-the-first-city?p=953175#post953175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I would say that's not based on any particular science out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would it be more appealing if I couched it as a psychic power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T08:01:49-07:00","id":953179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/951193-question-about-the-first-city?p=953168#post953168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Mokole actually had non-avian dinosaurs as kin (and attendant varnas) before the Wonder-Work of the Dissolver, and retain connections to everything that they remember.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm admittedly not overly familiar with the minutiae of the Mokole and odder Changing Breeds, but if they were dinosaur shifters what exactly did they shift <i>into</i> if they existed before humans? When does the &quot;were&quot; in were-lizard come into play?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T08:08:34-07:00","id":953181,"title":"","content":"A proto-humanoid akin to the Troodon dinosaurid, if memory serves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T08:28:34-07:00","id":953194,"title":"","content":"The Dinosaur Kings, a reptilian or dinosaur tool user. The Mokole may have only had two forms between the extinction of the Dinosaur Kings and the evolution of homids, though they may have associated with the Bird Kings and Pouch Kings when they were dominant (it is vague). The real strange thing is that the Rokea had only three forms before the evolution of homids, as there is no indication that they were interested in anything on land before the evolution of homids. The same thing may have been the case of the Ananasi, as they predate homids as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T08:43:56-07:00","id":953203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/951193-question-about-the-first-city?p=953194#post953194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dinosaur Kings, a reptilian or dinosaur tool user. The Mokole may have only had two forms between the extinction of the Dinosaur Kings and the evolution of homids, though they may have associated with the Bird Kings and Pouch Kings when they were dominant (it is vague). The real strange thing is that the Rokea had only three forms before the evolution of homids, as there is no indication that they were interested in anything on land before the evolution of homids. The same thing may have been the case of the Ananasi, as they predate homids as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Shattered Dreams says Rokea and Ananasi had Reptid form back then","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T10:48:11-07:00","id":953284,"title":"","content":"Cool, it makes more sense than the default. Is Shattered Dreams out yet? I could not tell on the website.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T11:02:08-07:00","id":953295,"title":"","content":"It's in proofing right now, backers haven't even received the pdf yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T13:43:24-07:00","id":953405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/951193-question-about-the-first-city?p=953284#post953284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool, it makes more sense than the default. Is Shattered Dreams out yet? I could not tell on the website.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, but you can still check out the previews at the KS","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}